    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d479">

                <pb facs="0648" n="556" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg556"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Food Administrator’s File</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Food Administrator</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hoover</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the British Ambassador on Special
                        Mission</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Reading</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 14, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Lord Reading</hi>: I greatly appreciate the
                    kindliness of your note of June 12 and I shall be honoured indeed to be the
                    guest of His Majesty’s Government.</p>
                <p>I do not expect to remain in Europe more than a fortnight as I believe that will
                    be sufficient time to discuss food programmes for next year, so far as they can
                    be determined in advance.</p>
                <p>I have a feeling that a personal conference with the food administrators abroad
                    would enable us to co-ordinate our problems of production, transportation and
                    supply to better advantage than last year, which has been more or less an
                    experimental and experience-gaining period.</p>
                <p>Yours faithfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Herbert Hoover</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
